 - **LV2, level script VM (2026-11-13, LEVELS round 2; docs/LEVELS.md "The level script VM"):** `core/src/lv_script.c` + `core/include/doomo/lv_script.h`: a deterministic bytecode interpreter (8 events, 20 actions, 32 byte variables, 16 actions a tick, 64 handlers / 2 KB, a queue of 16) with one host function for everything outside the VM; `tools/mapc.py` compiles `on EVENT [repeat] do ACTION ; ...` into `DoomoMapExt.script` and refuses what the VM would. Host tests per action and event, budgets, the checker, and a mapc-compiled script run twice with equal hashes. Nothing in the game calls it yet, so no byte on any platform (GBA sizes identical, PS1 EXE identical).
 - **Speed S3-2 (built 2026-11-15, partial; the CREATOR stream, speed audit 3; measured on libmgba and PCSX-Redux; docs/GBA.md "Speed wave 3: S3-2", docs/PORTRAIT.md "UI previews", docs/PS1.md "S3-2"):** a UI preview never draws a whole portrait, figure or chibi inside a frame (`portrait_image_ui` and friends: a patient job and NULL meanwhile, no 4-tick deadline; native and Dreamcast unchanged), the roster card and the studio picker prefetch the next and previous face, and a forced portrait slice runs only when it costs at most one more vblank (`pslice_policy.h`, GBA and PS1). GBA drawn fps before -> after: studio picker move 28.5 -> 30.0, shop cursor move 28.0 -> 30.0, shop gifts tab 29.5 -> 30.0, add-member pick move 25.4 -> 29.5, cook counter 18.3 -> 26.5, library lobby 19.6 -> 24.0; the quest log's Friends tab load 238 -> 41 ms, shop / cafe / Black Market / picker entries 118-136 -> 52-70 ms. GBA EWRAM / IWRAM unchanged (net zero against the tip: `.bss` 254,828 B, 6,420 B free); PS1 +304 B resident (132,608 -> 132,320 B below the stack top on the PS1-RAM tree). **Left:** entries still 41-70 ms (not under 34), creator entry / swatch / try-on windows unchanged, the title (S2-10's file), "dear slices cut finer", scene-start prefetch under the loading fade, a few more 50 ms frames in picker / Black Market windows. **Done:** UI previews as patient jobs, neighbour prefetch, the forced-slice rule.
 - **LV3 part 1, mechanic kit A: movement rules (2026-11-13, LEVELS round 3a; docs/LEVELS.md "Mechanic kit A, movement"):** `core/src/levels_mech_move.c`: ride cycles, ziplines, bounce pads + low gravity, carry, tubes and the raft as pure rules on a 16-byte `MmMove`, plus `mm_edges` (the same edges as the BFS) for the autopilot; kit test map `core/tests/maps/t3_kit.txt` and 17 host tests, among them a bot that plans over the BFS walk rule + `mm_edges` and plays the plan through the real state machine across the six mechanics (five edge kinds plus the low-gravity step). Nothing calls it yet (no resident byte on any platform). **Not yet (LV3 part 2):** the ride state in `combat.c`, the zone triggers in the runtime and the edges inside `combat_bot.c`, each with its Vape Cellar fps before / after.
-- **LV9, combat detail option in levels (2026-11-15, LEVELS-2; docs/LEVELS.md "The combat detail option in levels", plan 8.7 / 7.2):** `core/src/levels_detail.c` + `lv_detail.h`: dropped effects per mode and held pressure (a prefix of the level's `detail` list, one step at a time, 1.5 s of good frames to get one back), awake caps per mode and platform from the new `awake S B M` header key (defaults 6 / 8 / 10, PS1 x1.5, DC x2; mapc validates, GBA maps at most 6 8 10), five new append-only `MDET_*` kinds (steam, rain, crowd, decals, loot), Smooth loot / prop thinning that never drops a key, secret, collectible or quest thing. Hooks only in the existing option's places (`combat.c` spawn, `combat_scene.c` view detail), compiled out on the PS1; nothing feeds frame-cost pressure yet and no v2 level exists to use it. 13 core tests + 3 mapc tests. GBA: .iwram / .iwram_bss / .bss identical, ROM +584 B `.text`; Vape Cellar vhash-seq identical in all three modes, drawn fps equal (8.8 / 8.5 / 16.6, the speed stream's gap), start-room work +0.4..1.0 ms of 76.
+- **LV9, combat detail option in levels (2026-11-15, LEVELS-2; docs/LEVELS.md "The combat detail option in levels", plan 8.7 / 7.2):** `core/src/levels_detail.c` + `lv_detail.h`: dropped effects per mode and held pressure (a prefix of the level's `detail` list, one step at a time, 1.5 s of good frames to get one back), awake caps per mode and platform from the new `awake S B M` header key (defaults 6 / 8 / 10, PS1 x1.5, DC x2; mapc validates, GBA maps at most 6 8 10), five new append-only `MDET_*` kinds (steam, rain, crowd, decals, loot), Smooth loot / prop thinning that never drops a key, secret, collectible or quest thing. Hooks only in the existing option's places (`combat.c` spawn, `combat_scene.c` view detail), compiled out on the PS1; nothing feeds frame-cost pressure yet and no v2 level exists to use it. 9 core tests + 4 mapc tests. GBA: .iwram / .iwram_bss / .bss identical, ROM +584 B `.text`; Vape Cellar vhash-seq identical in all three modes, drawn fps equal (8.8 / 8.5 / 16.6, the speed stream's gap), start-room work +0.4..1.0 ms of 76.
 - **LV4, mechanic kit B: environment and light (2026-11-13, LEVELS round 3a; docs/LEVELS.md "Mechanic kit B"):** `core/src/levels_mech_env.c` + `lv_env.h`: fog zones with valves, the glum tide, lantern (25 cells) and candles, the Wall's two faces, the showtime light swap, collapsing floors and dissolving rooms, each rebuilt exactly from the definition (new zone kinds `candle`, `show`, `collapse`); per-level view distance (`DoomoView3D.view_dist`, header key `view`) in the native raycaster and the GBA `r3d.c`, PS1 compiled out until PS1-RAM (no resident byte), DC ignores it for now. 15 host tests incl. the renderer at both sizes. GBA RAM identical, speed tour frame-exact, PS1 EXE unchanged. Nothing calls it yet; the first level that needs a piece wires it (follow-up LV4b in `docs/design/held/status/LEVELS.md`).
 - **Speed S3-3 (2026-11-13, the creator, speed audit 3; measured on libmgba and PCSX-Redux; docs/CREATOR.md "S3-3", docs/GBA.md "Speed wave 3: S3-3", docs/PS1.md "S3-3"):** the held creator frame (the saved G2-CR work) and creator panels drawn on the fast path before their capture (S2-6's recipe, `plat_ui_loops` before the pane). GBA: grid scrolled 17.2 -> 26.8 fps, rows 29.4 -> 30.0, a value held 22.2 -> 29.4, the picker 22.7 -> 29.1, hat grid 27.2 -> 29.8, try-on 15.2 -> 26.9, filter chip 21.7 -> 30.5; four tab changes still have two 50 ms frames, the held grid and the try-on stay under 30 (each step is a whole new bust: S3-2). PS1: the grid keeps its unpacked icons in the overlay scratch, grid scrolled 29.39 -> 30.00, try-on 28.57 -> 29.03; no resident byte (64 KB below the stack top with the FMV). Settled screens byte-identical; the pane's in-between frames come a tick later.
 - **No 3D character models inside houses (PS1-FLAT, 2026-11-13; the owner: "disabled the 3d models of your player character and vice versa when you are inside their houses - save up some ram there", `OWNER_DECISIONS.md` "HOUSE CHARACTERS FLAT"; measured on PCSX-Redux; docs/PS1.md "No 3D models in houses", section 7):** only the PS1 drew a 3D figure in the house, the player's chibi (`model.c`). `ps1/src/room.c` now draws the player with the same `billboard()` as every resident, visitor, guest and demon, from the body sprite the core hands over (direction, walk frame, sit squash; the picture the GBA and the Dreamcast show, and the avatar being played), in Build, Live, Photo, Score, Hold the Door and a visit; it keeps its contact shadow and still rests in the kept backdrop while it stands still. With the house out, `model.c` (4,132 B) left resident RAM for the combat overlay group: `ovl_plan.py` `PLAT_GROUPS` / `GUARDED`, and `plat_view3d()` asks `ovl_code_in()` before it draws the model (the plan fails if house code, or anything else, would call it; `ps1/tools/test_ovl_guard.py`, 6 tests, in CI). The house's hooks in the 3D code are gone (`g_model_hold`, `g_r3_area`). **PS1 game disc with the boot FMV: 65,952 -> 70,480 B below the stack top (+4,528 B); on the tip it landed on (`19d01fe`) 68,224 -> 72,736 B (+4,512 B), 992 B under the 72 KB gate**; the slot keeps its 131,072 B (combat group 124,056 -> 128,188 B, home 130,856 -> 129,420 B). `prims.c` (3,612 B) stays resident: with it the combat group would pass the slot. House fps (`home.txt`, on the landing tip): plain 30.17 -> 30.17, steady 29.39 -> 30.00, orbit 27.17 -> 30.00, cellar (stress layout) 27.80 -> 27.80, defend stress (stress layout) 19.10 -> 22.78, modal 29.19 -> 30.00, Hold the Door wave 3 30.13 -> 30.13 (15.1 -> 6.5 ms of CPU), visit 30.17 -> 30.17; the speed tour's 19 house windows all hold 30 (the busy Live layout 28.78 -> 30.00). Third-person combat is unchanged: `perf_combat`'s shots are byte-identical, fps 29.5-30.0 as before. The core, the GBA and the Dreamcast are untouched (no file of theirs changed).
